      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Researchers typically look for signs of gentrification by tracking changes in socio-economic indicators such as rising property values, increased median household income, and a shift towards more affluent, white residents. They also examine the displacement of long-time, low-income, and minority residents, as evidenced by a decrease in the percentage of African American or Latino residents in the area. Additionally, they may look for an increase in upscale businesses, such as boutiques, art galleries, and restaurants, catering to the new, more affluent clientele. These changes often lead to a decline in the availability of affordable housing, community resources, and social services for the original residents.",
